<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">João Figueiredo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1999">1999</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as João Baptista Figueiredo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">João Figueiredo was a Brazilian general and the last president of the military dictatorship, serving from 1979 to 1985. He continued the gradual opening begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernesto-geisel">Ernesto Geisel</a>, granting an amnesty in 1979 and allowing the return of a multi-party system, and handed power to a civilian government in 1985.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joao-figueiredo.jpg" alt="João Figueiredo" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Governo do Brasil Original image uploader Sfs90 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jo%C3%A3o_Figueiredo,_presidente_do_Brasil,_1979_(vers%C3%A3o_colorida).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
